body:
I believe only `{ isError } = useQuery(...);` is VariableDeclarator and the whole `const { isError } = useQuery(...)` is VariableDeclaration. The same can be confirmed via the interfaces defined in estree package.
```
export interface VariableDeclaration extends BaseDeclaration {
    type: "VariableDeclaration";
    declarations: VariableDeclarator[];
    kind: "var" | "let" | "const" | "using" | "await using";
}

export interface VariableDeclarator extends BaseNode {
    type: "VariableDeclarator";
    id: Pattern;
    init?: Expression | null | undefined;
}
```
According to this accessing def.node will be as if accessing the VariableDeclarator.

