body:
`errorRecovery` uses a module-scoped `hasEncounteredError` closure, so its state persists across story/test runs even after `worker.resetHandlers()`. That can make later runs unexpectedly skip the simulated error. Prefer modeling this as a Scenario (there’s already `S3EdgeConfigUpdateWithErrorRecoveryScenario`) or make the handler stateless and keep state in scenario instance with teardown reset.
```suggestion
